{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>He who acquires</b> — (עד): two binders [i.e., maqqef pairs]. [The word] 'knowledge' is called 'heart.' 'He who loves his soul' — to keep it alive 'until the time of old age.'" "<b>And he who keeps understanding</b> — after he has acquired it, in order to find good he keeps it, for HaShem will bring him his good in this world and in the world to come. But 'he who hates' [i.e., one who has not] acquired knowledge will not be clear from destruction."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:38.002418121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}